AGA survey: 82% of Americans want prediction markets regulated as gambling

A survey commissioned by the American Gaming Association found that 82% of US voters think sports contracts on prediction markets should be regulated as gambling, not as financial products like swaps or futures. Support was similar across parties: 84% of Democrats, 82% of Republicans and 80% of independents. About 75% said betting on a prediction market is essentially the same as using a sportsbook. The online poll covered 2,268 registered voters aged 21+ and ran September 2–18, as states including Louisiana and Massachusetts pursue lawsuits against prediction-market operators.

